1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,500
大家好
Hello, everyone.

2
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:11,700
欢迎来到《一句英语，一个故事》
Welcome to One Phrase, One Story.

3
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:14,300
我是 Pastor Paul
I am Pastor Paul.

4
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:17,300
每天花几分钟的时间
Spend a few minutes each day.

5
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:20,000
学习一句地道的英语
Learn a natural English expression.

6
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:22,100
听一个经典的故事
Listen to a classic story.

7
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:25,600
你会发现文化背后的
Discover what lies behind the culture:

8
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:27,900
智慧人生
wisdom for life.

9
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:31,100
今天我们要学习的是
Today we are going to learn...

10
00:00:31,787 --> 00:00:33,207
伊甸园
The Garden of Eden.

11
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:36,260
如果你已经拥有一个美好的家园，
What if you already had a beautiful home,

12
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:41,060
有清新的空气、丰盛的果实，还有可以信赖的关系，
fresh air, abundant fruit, and relationships you could trust?

13
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:42,900
你还会失去什么？
What could you still lose?

14
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:46,280
今天的故事，不只关乎一个地方，
Today's story is about more than a place.

15
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:48,980
更关乎人为什么会失去归属，
It asks why we can lose our sense of belonging,

16
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:52,860
又为什么始终向往一个可以安心生活的家。
and why we long for a home where we can live in peace.

17
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:56,453
《创世记》第二章描绘了一座园子：
Genesis chapter 2 describes a garden:

18
00:00:56,673 --> 00:01:01,633
各种悦人眼目、好作食物的树木从地里长出来，
trees grew that were beautiful to look at and good for food,

19
00:01:01,873 --> 00:01:03,933
有河流滋润园子。
and a river watered the garden.

20
00:01:03,933 --> 00:01:07,533
人被安置在那里，修理、看守这个地方。
The man was placed there to work the garden and care for it.

21
00:01:07,973 --> 00:01:10,593
伊甸园并不意味着什么都不用做。
Eden did not mean having nothing to do.

22
00:01:10,973 --> 00:01:14,053
美好的生活，也包含照顾和守护。
A good life also included care and stewardship.

23
00:01:14,413 --> 00:01:18,067
人在其中，不只是享用者，也是受托的人。
The human being was not only a recipient, but also a caretaker.

24
00:01:18,633 --> 00:01:21,973
园中的生活有自由，也有界限。
Life in the garden included both freedom and boundaries.

25
00:01:21,973 --> 00:01:25,433
上帝准许人吃园中各样树上的果子，
God allowed the man to eat from the trees of the garden,

26
00:01:25,573 --> 00:01:29,433
却吩咐他不可吃分别善恶树上的果子。
but not from the tree of the knowledge of good and evil.

27
00:01:29,593 --> 00:01:33,393
这条界限，使自由与责任同时进入故事。
This boundary brought freedom and responsibility into the story.

28
00:01:33,733 --> 00:01:36,633
后来，蛇的诱惑使人开始怀疑：
Later, the serpent's temptation invited doubt:

29
00:01:36,893 --> 00:01:38,913
眼前的美好，是否还不够？
Was the goodness they already had somehow not enough?

30
00:01:38,913 --> 00:01:42,493
设下界限的那一位，是否真的值得信任？
Could the one who set the boundary really be trusted?

31
00:01:43,187 --> 00:01:45,927
当亚当和夏娃越过那条界限，
When Adam and Eve crossed that boundary,

32
00:01:46,147 --> 00:01:48,527
改变的不只是他们吃了什么。
more changed than what they had eaten.

33
00:01:48,807 --> 00:01:53,687
他们开始遮掩自己，躲避上帝，并把责任推向别人。
They covered themselves, hid from God, and shifted responsibility.

34
00:01:54,147 --> 00:01:58,927
园中的树木仍在那里，但关系里的坦然已经失去了。
The trees remained, but openness in their relationships was lost.

35
00:01:58,927 --> 00:02:02,667
一个地方能成为家，不只因为风景优美，
A place becomes home through more than beautiful scenery.

36
00:02:02,927 --> 00:02:06,367
也因为人在其中能够信任，不必躲藏。
It is also a place where we can trust, without needing to hide.

37
00:02:06,713 --> 00:02:11,613
故事最后，他们离开了伊甸园，面对园外的劳苦生活。
At the end, they left Eden to face the hardships of life outside.

38
00:02:11,893 --> 00:02:14,993
经文也记载，上帝为他们做了衣服。
The text also says that God made garments for them.

39
00:02:15,213 --> 00:02:18,233
这让离开的画面不只是风景的转换，
Their departure was more than a change of scenery:

40
00:02:18,373 --> 00:02:21,033
而是一个不再能轻易返回的家。
they had lost a home to which they could not simply return.

41
00:02:21,493 --> 00:02:25,213
从此，伊甸园也成为人们谈论失去的美好、
Eden became a cultural image for lost beauty

42
00:02:25,433 --> 00:02:28,653
理想家园时，常常借用的文化意象。
and the longing for an ideal home.

43
00:02:29,727 --> 00:02:32,727
今天的表达，字面意思是伊甸园。
Today's expression literally names the biblical Garden of Eden.

44
00:02:33,047 --> 00:02:38,727
在现代英语里，它也可以比喻一个美丽、宁静、令人向往的地方。
In modern English, it can also describe a beautiful, peaceful, desirable place.

45
00:02:38,927 --> 00:02:41,907
注意，这是一种带有文学色彩的比喻。
Notice that this is a literary metaphor.

46
00:02:42,227 --> 00:02:45,767
说到圣经中的那座园子，我们用定冠词。
We use the definite article for the particular biblical garden.

47
00:02:45,767 --> 00:02:50,447
描述某个像天堂一样的地方时，也可以用不定冠词。
For a place imagined as an earthly paradise, the indefinite article can work too.

48
00:02:50,787 --> 00:02:52,000
听听这两个例句。
Listen to these two examples.

49
00:02:52,627 --> 00:02:57,167
第一个例句：这个宁静的山谷，看起来就像伊甸园。
Example one: the quiet valley looked like Eden.

50
00:02:57,833 --> 00:03:01,113
这个宁静的山谷看起来就像伊甸园。
The peaceful valley looked like the Garden of Eden.

51
00:03:02,433 --> 00:03:05,713
这个宁静的山谷看起来就像伊甸园。
The peaceful valley looked like the Garden of Eden.

52
00:03:09,453 --> 00:03:15,153
第二个例句：他们梦想把自家的后院，变成一个美丽的伊甸园。
Example two: they dreamed of making their backyard into a paradise.

53
00:03:15,627 --> 00:03:19,733
他们梦想把自家的后院变成一个美丽的伊甸园。
They dreamed of turning their backyard into a Garden of Eden.

54
00:03:20,893 --> 00:03:25,000
他们梦想把自家的后院变成一个美丽的伊甸园。
They dreamed of turning their backyard into a Garden of Eden.

55
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:30,520
前一句用伊甸园作比较，
The first sentence uses Eden as a comparison.

56
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:34,960
后一句把自家后院想象成一处理想天地。
The second imagines a backyard as an ideal place.

57
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:39,500
你不必拥有一座真正的乐园，也可以用这个表达，
You need not own a paradise to use this expression

58
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:42,333
描绘一片让人感到安宁的地方。
for a place that gives people a sense of peace.

59
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:47,800
这个故事带来的问题是：我们怎样对待已经拥有的美好？
The story asks: how do we treat the good things we already have?

60
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:50,980
再好的环境，也不能代替信任；
Even the finest surroundings cannot replace trust.

61
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:53,920
再舒适的家，也需要有人照顾。
Even the most comfortable home needs care.

62
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:57,560
真正的幸福，不仅在于拥有美好的环境，
Happiness depends on more than beautiful surroundings.

63
00:03:57,700 --> 00:04:01,340
也在于懂得珍惜、信任与承担责任。
It also calls for appreciation, trust, and responsibility.

64
00:04:01,880 --> 00:04:04,320
也许，守护身边的人和事，
Perhaps caring for the people and things around us

65
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:06,940
就是让一个地方更像家的开始。
is how we begin to make a place feel more like home.

66
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:12,433
今天的表达是伊甸园。请再听一次，然后跟读。
Today's expression is the Garden of Eden. Listen again, then repeat.

67
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:14,140
伊甸园
The Garden of Eden.

68
00:04:15,187 --> 00:04:16,607
伊甸园
The Garden of Eden.

69
00:04:18,833 --> 00:04:24,733
一句英语，一个故事。我是 Paul Zhang 张崇助。我们下次再见。
One Phrase, One Story. I'm Paul Zhang. See you next time.
